-- name: Files touched outside any declared plan
-- class: Consistency
-- metric: alignment_collect_d1
-- action: declare the touched files in a slice or plan, or confirm the out-of-plan work was deliberate scope
-- severity: WARN
-- guardrail: BOTH SIDES OF THIS DISAGREEMENT LIVE IN alignment-collect's OWN d1 RECORD -- spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-30-loopsmith-insight-data-platform-design.md:529's own parenthetical names d1 files_changed_outside_any_plan directly; alignment-collect.sh's own printf (lines 445-446) emits commits_with_source and files_changed_outside_any_plan together in one object, so no join is needed or possible. POPULATION IS SCOPED TO PACKS THAT ACTUALLY CARRY A d1 BLOCK (json_extract(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d1') IS NOT NULL), NOT MERELY THE RIGHT schema -- the same false-PASS defense as the sibling consistency_verify_no_test_touched.sql rule, proven live against the identical trap (.sdlc/plans/120.md Design decision 3 / Key facts item 3): a store whose packs lack d1 entirely reads population 0, not a false non-zero. THE EVIDENCE ARRAY COLUMN IS A DIRECT CAST(... AS VARCHAR[]) OF THE JSON ARRAY -- proven live this session to return a native Python list through the DB-API with no UNNEST needed (Design decision 4), matching coverage_gate_absent.sql's/coverage_degraded_collector.sql's own array-evidence precedent for degraded_collector/degraded_adapter; this is new idiom for a raw_payload-derived array specifically (no existing metric or rule had ever surfaced one before this story -- 20.sql explodes its own churn_hotspots array via from_json/unnest instead of returning it directly). REQUIRES commits_with_source > 0 (an existence check, not a magnitude) SO A PACK WITH NO REAL SOURCE ACTIVITY NEVER FIRES ON A STALE OR EMPTY ARRAY -- COALESCE(json_array_length(...), 0) > 0 mirrors 30.sql's own COALESCE(len(...), 0) array-emptiness idiom, adapted to json_array_length because the value here is a JSON value extracted from raw_payload, not yet a native VARCHAR[] column. files_outside_plan_confidence IS CARRIED THROUGH AS AN HONEST, NON-GATING, INFORMATIONAL COLUMN -- alignment-collect.sh itself always emits "low" here today (its own printf line 445), never varying per pack, so this rule's WHERE clause never reads or gates on it (there is only one value it could ever be); it is surfaced purely so a consumer sees the upstream heuristic's own stated low confidence right in the evidence row (Design decision 6), the same passthrough posture coverage_gate_absent.sql already established for degraded_collector/degraded_adapter. WHY d1-SOURCED RATHER THAN A fact_slice JOIN -- fact_slice has a real writer (artifact_reader.py's write_slices) but no join key to any commit or collector-pack row: a slice's own files[] is a plan-time declaration with no timestamp or commit-sha correlation to d1's observed per-commit file list, and this repo has no .slices.json at all today; alignment-collect.sh already performs the file-vs-plan correlation this rule needs (its own found_in_plan logic, lines ~323-337), so this rule reads that already-computed result rather than re-deriving it against a disconnected table (Design decision 3's rejected alternative). MALFORMED-PAYLOAD DISCLOSURE (systemic, pre-existing, not fixed here): a fact_collector_pack row whose schema = 'alignment-collect/v1' and whose raw_payload is non-NULL but not valid JSON makes every json_extract call in this rule's population and evidence queries raise DuckDB's InvalidInputException, crashing evaluate_rule rather than degrading to ABSENT -- the identical, unguarded json_extract(raw_payload, ...) pattern every one of the six already-shipped rules (and metrics 5/20/24/41) already shares. This fails LOUD, not silent, so it is not a false PASS and is not spec:534's forbidden collapse; widening scope to guard every json_extract call across the catalog against a malformed payload is out of this story's scope (see .sdlc/plans/120.md Risks).
-- population: SELECT count(*) FROM fact_collector_pack WHERE schema = 'alignment-collect/v1' AND json_extract(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d1') IS NOT NULL
SELECT
    project_id,
    collected_ts,
    CAST(json_extract(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d1.commits_with_source') AS INTEGER) AS commits_with_source,
    CAST(json_extract(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d1.files_changed_outside_any_plan') AS VARCHAR[]) AS files_changed_outside_any_plan,
    json_extract_string(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d1.files_outside_plan_confidence') AS files_outside_plan_confidence
FROM fact_collector_pack
WHERE schema = 'alignment-collect/v1'
  AND COALESCE(CAST(json_extract(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d1.commits_with_source') AS INTEGER), 0) > 0
  AND COALESCE(json_array_length(json_extract(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d1.files_changed_outside_any_plan')), 0) > 0
ORDER BY project_id, collected_ts
